## Pattern observed

Most misses are LONG, multi-segment strings with one or more of:

1. **Word doc whitespace divergence:** the LLM-extracted text has single spaces where the
   source document has line breaks, tabs, multi-space gaps, NBSPs, or table-cell boundaries.
   Frontend search variants only try `as-is`, `no-space`, `spaced-letter`. None of them
   normalise *internal* whitespace flexibly.
2. **Casing divergence:** `KALUPUR POLICE STATION` (LLM, all-caps) vs `KALUPUR Police Station`
   (doc, mixed-case) — earlier in the same log, the mixed-case form was found because that
   was the LLM's exact extraction; the all-caps variant was never tried.
3. **Punctuation rendering:** smart quotes (`"…''`), em-dash vs hyphen, trailing colons
   pulled into the value (`Date :29/06/2023`).
4. **Already-wrapped overlap:** `Section 138 of The Negotiable Instruments Act 1881` was
   wrapped successfully; later `Section:138 of The Negotiable Instruments Act : 1881`
   matched but its occurrence-0 was skipped (`already inside a content control`) because it
   physically overlaps the earlier wrap.

## Variables that succeeded

Single-token / short-span values (`HARIJAN BASTI`, `JODHPUR`, `AHMEDABAD`, `TOPS TEXTILES`,
`UCO BANK`, `RJ902`, deterministic-extractor outputs `08BLGPS7568P1ZX`,
`bgrpadvocate@gmail.com`, `28/06/2023`, `UBIN0531294`) all wrapped.

